# Verified summaries from rendered pages of the supplied DMG. Pages use PDF numbering.
DATA = {
'Boots of Speed': (243,'Wondrous Item, Rare','Yes',"While wearing the boots, take a Bonus Action to click the heels together. Your Speed doubles, and creatures making Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage on those attack rolls. Clicking your heels together again ends the effect. After a total of 10 minutes of use, the boots stop functioning until you finish a Long Rest."),
'Boots of Striding and Springing': (243,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the boots, your Speed becomes 30 feet unless it is already higher. Carrying more than your carrying capacity or wearing Heavy Armor doesn't reduce your Speed. Once on each of your turns, you can jump up to 30 feet by spending only 10 feet of movement."),
'Boots of the Winterlands': (243,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing these furred boots, you have Resistance to Cold damage and can tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower without additional protection. You ignore Difficult Terrain created by ice or snow."),
'Bowl of Commanding Water Elementals': (243,'Wondrous Item, Rare','No',"While the bowl is filled with water and you are within 5 feet of it, take a Magic action to summon a Water Elemental in an unoccupied space as close to the bowl as possible. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The bowl can't summon another elemental until the next dawn. The bowl is about 1 foot in diameter and half as deep, and holds about 3 gallons."),
'Bracers of Archery': (243,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the bracers, you have proficiency with the Longbow and Shortbow and gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls made with those weapons."),
'Bracers of Defense': (244,'Wondrous Item, Rare','Yes',"While wearing the bracers, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class if you are wearing no armor and using no Shield."),
'Brazier of Commanding Fire Elementals': (244,'Wondrous Item, Rare','No',"While within 5 feet of the brazier, take a Magic action to summon a Fire Elemental in an unoccupied space as close to the brazier as possible. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The brazier can't summon another elemental until the next dawn."),
'Brooch of Shielding': (244,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the brooch, you have Resistance to Force damage and Immunity to damage from the Magic Missile spell."),
'Broom of Flying': (244,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"Stand astride this wooden broom and take a Magic action to make it hover beneath you. It has a Fly Speed of 50 feet and can carry up to 400 pounds; its Fly Speed becomes 30 feet while carrying more than 200 pounds. It stops hovering when you land or are no longer riding it.\n\nAs a Magic action, send the broom to a destination within 1 mile by naming a location you are familiar with. If the broom is still within 1 mile, another Magic action and a command word call it back to you."),
'Candle of Invocation': (244,'Wondrous Item, Very Rare','Yes',"Lighting the candle takes a Magic action and activates its magic. It is destroyed after a total of 4 hours of burning. You can snuff it early for later use; deduct expended time in increments of 1 minute. While lit, it sheds Dim Light in a 30-foot radius. You and your allies in the light have Advantage on D20 Tests. A Cleric or Druid in the light can also cast prepared level 1 spells without expending spell slots."),
'Chime of Opening': (247,'Wondrous Item, Rare','No',"This hollow metal tube is about 1 foot long and weighs 1 pound. As a Magic action, strike it to cast Knock. Instead of the spell's normal knocking sound, the chime rings clearly and is audible up to 300 feet. It can be used 10 times; after the tenth use it cracks and becomes useless."),
'Circlet of Blasting': (247,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','No',"While wearing the circlet, you can cast Scorching Ray from it with a +5 attack bonus. The circlet can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."),
'Cloak of Arachnida': (247,'Wondrous Item, Very Rare','Yes',"While wearing this black silk cloak, you gain the following benefits.\n\n- **Poison Resistance.** You have Resistance to Poison damage.\n- **Spider Climb.** You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed and can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings while leaving your hands free.\n- **Spider Walk.** You can't be caught in webs of any sort, and move through webs as though they were Difficult Terrain.\n- **Web.** You can cast Web (save DC 13). Its web fills twice its normal area. This property recharges at the next dawn."),
'Cloak of Displacement': (247,'Wondrous Item, Rare','Yes',"While wearing the cloak, an illusion makes you appear to stand near your actual location. Creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. If you take damage, this property stops functioning until the start of your next turn. It is suppressed while your Speed is 0."),
'Cloak of Elvenkind': (247,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the cloak, Wisdom (Perception) checks made to perceive you have Disadvantage, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks."),
'Cloak of Invisibility': (247,'Wondrous Item, Legendary','Yes',"The cloak has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, take a Magic action to pull its hood over your head and expend 1 charge to give yourself the Invisible condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you pull the hood down (no action required) or cease wearing the cloak."),
'Eyes of Charming': (264,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"These crystal lenses have 3 charges. While wearing them, expend 1 or more charges to cast Charm Person (save DC 13). One charge casts the level 1 version; each additional charge increases the spell's level by one. The lenses regain all expended charges daily at dawn."),
'Eyes of Minute Seeing': (264,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','No',"While wearing these crystal lenses, you have Darkvision to a range of 1 foot and Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks to examine something within that range."),
'Pearl of Power': (287,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes, by a spellcaster',"While the pearl is on your person, take a Magic action to regain one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower. Once used, the pearl can't be used again until the next dawn."),
'Periapt of Health': (287,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the pendant, take a Magic action to regain 2d4 + 2 Hit Points. This property recharges at the next dawn. In addition, while wearing it you have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Poisoned condition."),
'Periapt of Proof against Poison': (287,'Wondrous Item, Rare','Yes',"While wearing this pendant, you have Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition."),
'Potion of Growth': (291,'Potion, Uncommon','No',"Drinking the potion gives you the enlarge effect of Enlarge/Reduce for 10 minutes, without requiring Concentration."),
'Potion of Heroism': (291,'Potion, Rare','No',"Drinking the potion gives you 10 Temporary Hit Points that last for 1 hour. For that hour, you also benefit from Bless without requiring Concentration."),
'Potion of Invisibility': (291,'Potion, Rare','No',"Drinking the potion gives you the Invisible condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell."),
'Potion of Invulnerability': (291,'Potion, Rare','No',"For 1 minute after drinking the potion, you have Resistance to all damage."),
'Potion of Longevity': (291,'Potion, Very Rare','No',"Drinking the potion reduces your physical age by 1d6 + 6 years, to a minimum of 13 years. Each subsequent Potion of Longevity you drink has a cumulative 10 percent chance of instead aging you by 1d6 + 6 years."),
'Potion of Mind Reading': (291,'Potion, Rare','No',"Drinking the potion gives you the effect of Detect Thoughts (save DC 13) for 10 minutes, without requiring Concentration."),
'Ring of Spell Storing': (298,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"The ring stores up to 5 levels of spells. When found, it contains 1d6 - 1 levels of stored spells chosen by the DM. Any creature can store a level 1-5 spell by touching the ring while casting it. The spell has no other effect. If it won't fit, the spell is expended without effect. Storage used equals the level of the spell slot used.\n\nWhile wearing the ring, you can cast any stored spell. It uses the original caster's slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability; otherwise you are the caster. Casting removes that spell from the ring and frees its space."),
'Ring of Spell Turning': (298,'Ring, Legendary','Yes',"While wearing the ring, you have Advantage on saving throws against spells. If you succeed on the save against a spell of level 7 or lower, that spell has no effect on you. If it targeted only you and did not create an area of effect, you can take a Reaction to deflect it back at its caster. The caster must save against the spell using their own spell save DC."),
'Ring of Swimming': (298,'Ring, Uncommon','No',"While wearing the ring, you have a Swim Speed of 40 feet."),
'Ring of Telekinesis': (298,'Ring, Very Rare','Yes',"While wearing the ring, you can cast Telekinesis from it."),
'Ring of the Ram': (299,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"The ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, take a Magic action and expend 1-3 charges to make a ranged spell attack against a creature you can see within 60 feet. The spectral ram attacks with a +7 bonus. On a hit, each expended charge deals 2d10 Force damage and pushes the target 5 feet away.\n\nAlternatively, expend 1-3 charges as a Magic action to try to break a nonmagical object you can see within 60 feet that isn't worn or carried. The ring makes a Strength check with a +5 bonus for each expended charge."),
'Ring of Three Wishes': (299,'Ring, Legendary','No',"While wearing the ring, expend 1 of its 3 charges to cast Wish. The ring becomes nonmagical when its last charge is used."),
'Ring of Warmth': (299,'Ring, Uncommon','Yes',"Whenever you take Cold damage while wearing the ring, reduce that damage by 2d8. In addition, you and everything you wear and carry are unharmed by temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower."),
'Ring of Water Walking': (299,'Ring, Uncommon','No',"While wearing the ring, you can cast Water Walk from it, targeting only yourself."),
'Ring of X-ray Vision': (299,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"While wearing the ring, take a Magic action to gain X-ray vision with a 30-foot range for 1 minute. Solid objects in that radius appear transparent to you and don't block light from passing through them. You can see through 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or up to 3 feet of wood or dirt. Thicker substances and thin sheets of lead block the vision.\n\nEach time you use this property again before taking a Long Rest, make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level."),
'Shield of Missile Attraction': (307,'Armor (Shield), Rare','Yes',"While holding the Shield, you have Resistance to damage from attacks made with Ranged weapons.\n\n**Curse.** Attuning to the Shield curses you until you are targeted by Remove Curse or similar magic. Removing the Shield does not end the curse. Whenever an attack with a Ranged weapon targets a creature within 10 feet of you, you become the target instead."),
'Shield of the Cavalier': (307,'Armor (Shield), Very Rare','Yes',"While holding the Shield, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class in addition to the Shield's normal bonus, and can use these properties.\n\n**Forceful Bash.** When you take the Attack action, one attack can be a Shield attack against a target within 5 feet. Add your Proficiency Bonus and Strength modifier to the attack roll. A hit deals 2d6 + 2 plus your Strength modifier in Force damage. You can push a creature hit up to 10 feet directly away; if it is your size or smaller, you can also give it the Prone condition.\n\n**Protective Field.** As a Reaction when you or an ally you can see within 5 feet is targeted by an attack or makes a saving throw against an area of effect, create an immobile 5-foot Emanation originating from you. Creatures and objects not fully contained within it are pushed to the nearest unoccupied spaces outside. The triggering attack or area of effect has no effect on creatures and objects inside. The Emanation lasts while you maintain Concentration, up to 1 minute. Nothing can pass into or out of it. Creatures and objects inside can't be damaged by attacks or effects originating outside, and creatures inside can't damage anything outside. This property recharges at the next dawn."),
'Animated Shield': (232,'Armor (Shield), Very Rare','Yes',"While holding the Shield, take a Bonus Action to animate it. It hovers in your space and protects you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. It remains animated for 1 minute, until you end the effect with a Bonus Action, or until you die or have the Incapacitated condition. It then falls to the ground or into a free hand."),
}
DATA.update({
'Periapt of Wound Closure': ([287,288],'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the pendant, you gain two benefits.\n\n**Life Preservation.** Whenever you make a Death Saving Throw, you can change a roll of 9 or lower to a 10, turning a failed save into a successful one.\n\n**Natural Healing Boost.** Whenever you roll a Hit Point Die to regain Hit Points, double the number of Hit Points it restores."),
'Philter of Love': (288,'Potion, Uncommon','No',"The next time you see a creature within 10 minutes after drinking the philter, you are charmed by that creature and have the Charmed condition for 1 hour."),
'Pipes of Haunting': (288,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','No',"The pipes have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. Take a Magic action to play them and expend 1 charge. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition for 1 minute. A creature that fails repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that succeeds is immune to these pipes' effect for 24 hours."),
'Pipes of the Sewers': (288,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While the pipes are on your person, ordinary and giant rats are Indifferent toward you and won't attack unless you threaten or harm them. The pipes have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.\n\nIf you play the pipes as a Magic action, you can take a Bonus Action to expend 1-3 charges, calling one Swarm of Rats per charge if the DM determines there are enough rats within half a mile. A charge is wasted if there are too few rats. Called swarms move toward the music by the shortest available route but are not otherwise under your control.\n\nWhenever a Swarm of Rats not controlled by another creature comes within 30 feet while you play, it makes a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a success, it behaves normally and can't be swayed by the music for 24 hours."),
'Potion of Poison': ([291,292],'Potion, Uncommon','No',"The potion looks, smells, and tastes like a Potion of Healing or another beneficial potion; illusion magic masks its true nature. Identify reveals the deception. Drinking it deals 4d6 Poison damage and requires a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, you have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour."),
'Potion of Speed': (292,'Potion, Very Rare','No',"Drinking the potion gives you the effect of Haste for 1 minute without Concentration. You do not suffer the wave of lethargy that normally occurs when the effect ends."),
'Potion of Vitality': (292,'Potion, Very Rare','No',"Drinking the potion removes all your Exhaustion levels and ends the Poisoned condition on you. For the next 24 hours, any Hit Point Die you spend restores its maximum number of Hit Points."),
'Potion of Water Breathing': (292,'Potion, Uncommon','No',"You can breathe underwater for 24 hours after drinking the potion."),
'Slippers of Spider Climbing': ([307,308],'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing these light shoes, you have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed and can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings while keeping your hands free. The slippers do not allow this movement on slippery surfaces, such as surfaces covered by ice or oil."),
'Sovereign Glue': (308,'Wondrous Item, Legendary','No',"This adhesive permanently bonds two objects. Store it in a jar or flask coated inside with Oil of Slipperiness. A found container holds 1d6 + 1 ounces. One ounce covers a 1-foot-square surface. Applying an ounce takes a Utilize action, and the glue takes 1 minute to set. Once set, its bond can be broken only by Universal Solvent, Oil of Etherealness, or Wish."),
'Spellguard Shield': (308,'Armor (Shield), Very Rare','Yes',"While holding the Shield, you have Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects. Spell attack rolls have Disadvantage against you."),
'Headband of Intellect': (271,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"Your Intelligence is 19 while wearing the headband. It has no effect if your Intelligence is already 19 or higher without it."),
'Helm of Telepathy': (271,'Wondrous Item, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the helm, you have Telepathy to a range of 30 feet and can cast Detect Thoughts or Suggestion (save DC 13) from it. Once either spell is cast from the helm, the helm can't cast that spell again until the next dawn."),
'Helm of Teleportation': (271,'Wondrous Item, Rare','Yes',"The helm has 3 charges. While wearing it, expend 1 charge to cast Teleport. It regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."),
'Ring of Evasion': (296,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"The ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. When you fail a Dexterity saving throw while wearing it, take a Reaction and expend 1 charge to succeed on that save instead."),
'Ring of Feather Falling': (296,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"When you fall while wearing the ring, you descend 60 feet per round and take no damage from falling."),
'Ring of Free Action': (296,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"While wearing the ring, Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement. Magic can neither reduce any of your Speeds nor cause you to have the Paralyzed or Restrained condition."),
'Ring of Invisibility': (296,'Ring, Legendary','Yes',"While wearing the ring, take a Magic action to give yourself the Invisible condition. It lasts until the ring is removed or you take a Bonus Action to become visible again."),
'Ring of Jumping': (296,'Ring, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the ring, you can cast Jump from it, targeting only yourself."),
'Ring of Mind Shielding': (296,'Ring, Uncommon','Yes',"While wearing the ring, you are immune to magic that reads your thoughts, determines whether you are lying, or reveals your alignment or creature type. Other creatures can communicate telepathically with you only if you allow it.\n\nTake a Magic action to make the ring imperceptible. It remains so until you take another Magic action to make it perceptible, remove it, or die."),
'Elixir of Health': (260,'Potion, Rare','No',"Drinking the potion cures all magical contagions and ends the Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, and Poisoned conditions on you."),
'Elven Chain': (260,'Armor (Chain Mail or Chain Shirt), Rare','No',"While wearing the armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class. You are considered trained with this armor even if you lack training with Medium or Heavy armor."),
'Universal Solvent': (321,'Wondrous Item, Legendary','No',"A found tube contains 1d6 + 1 ounces. Take a Utilize action to pour one or more ounces onto a surface within reach. Each ounce instantly dissolves up to 1 square foot of adhesive it touches, including Sovereign Glue."),
'Vicious Weapon': (321,'Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare','No',"This magic weapon deals an extra 2d6 damage to any creature it hits. The extra damage has the same type as the weapon's normal damage."),
'Wand of Binding': ([321,322],'Wand, Rare','Yes',"The wand has 7 charges. While holding it, expend 2 charges to cast Hold Person or 5 charges to cast Hold Monster (save DC 17). It regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll 1d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."),
'Wand of Enemy Detection': (322,'Wand, Rare','Yes',"The wand has 7 charges. While holding it, take a Magic action and expend 1 charge. For 1 minute, you know the direction, but not the distance, of the nearest creature Hostile to you within 60 feet. It detects Hostile creatures that are Invisible, ethereal, disguised, hidden, or in plain sight. The effect ends if you stop holding the wand.\n\nIt regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll 1d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."),
'Wand of Fear': (322,'Wand, Rare','Yes',"The wand has 7 charges. While holding it, expend 1 charge to cast Command (only the flee or grovel options) or 3 charges to cast Fear with a 60-foot Cone (save DC 15). It regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll 1d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."),
'Wand of Fireballs': (322,'Wand, Rare','Yes, by a spellcaster',"The wand has 7 charges. While holding it, expend 1-3 charges to cast Fireball (save DC 15). One charge casts the level 3 version; each additional charge increases the spell's level by 1. It regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll 1d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."),
'Wand of Paralysis': (324,'Wand, Rare','Yes, by a spellcaster',"The wand has 7 charges. While holding it, take a Magic action and expend 1 charge to target a creature you can see within 60 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Paralyzed condition for 1 minute. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nThe wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll 1d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."),
'Wand of Polymorph': (324,'Wand, Very Rare','Yes, by a spellcaster',"The wand has 7 charges. While holding it, expend 1 charge to cast Polymorph (save DC 15). It regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll 1d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."),
'Staff of Withering': (315,'Staff, Rare','Yes',"The staff has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. Wield it as a magic Quarterstaff, dealing normal Quarterstaff damage on a hit. When you hit, you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic damage and force the target to make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, it has Disadvantage on Strength and Constitution ability checks and saving throws for 1 hour."),
'Stone of Controlling Earth Elementals': (315,'Wondrous Item, Rare','No',"While touching this 5-pound stone to the ground, take a Magic action to summon an Earth Elemental in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet. It obeys your commands and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The stone can't summon another elemental until the next dawn."),
'Sun Blade': (315,'Weapon (Longsword), Rare','Yes',"**Blade of Radiance.** While grasping the hilt, take a Bonus Action to create or dismiss its radiant blade. With the blade present, it functions as a magic Longsword with the Finesse property. Proficiency with Longswords or Shortswords grants proficiency with the Sun Blade. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it; it deals Radiant damage instead of Slashing. A hit against an Undead deals an extra 1d8 Radiant damage.\n\n**Sunlight.** The blade emits sunlight as Bright Light within 15 feet and Dim Light for another 15 feet. While it exists, take a Magic action to increase or decrease both radii by 5 feet each, to a minimum of 10 feet each or a maximum of 30 feet each."),
})
SCROLL_RULES="A Spell Scroll holds one spell in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your spell list, you can read and cast it without Material components; otherwise the scroll is unintelligible. Use the spell's normal casting time. The scroll crumbles to dust when the spell is cast; interrupting the casting does not destroy it.\n\nIf the spell is on your list but is a higher level than you can normally cast, make an ability check using your spellcasting ability, with DC 10 + the spell's level. On a failure, the spell disappears from the scroll without effect."
TABLE=[('Cantrip','Common',13,5),('1','Common',13,5),('2','Uncommon',13,5),('3','Uncommon',15,7),('4','Rare',15,7),('5','Rare',17,9),('6','Very Rare',17,9),('7','Very Rare',18,10),('8','Very Rare',18,10),('9','Legendary',19,11)]
DATA['Spell Scroll']=(308,'Scroll, Rarity Varies','No',SCROLL_RULES+'\n\n| Spell level | Rarity | Save DC | Attack bonus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'+'\n'.join(f'| {l} | {r} | {d} | +{a} |' for l,r,d,a in TABLE))
for level,rarity,dc,attack in TABLE:
 name='Cantrip Spell Scroll' if level=='Cantrip' else f'Level {level} Spell Scroll'
 DATA[name]=(308,'Scroll, '+rarity,'No',f'**Spell level:** {level}  \n**Spell save DC:** {dc}  \n**Spell attack bonus:** +{attack}\n\n'+SCROLL_RULES+'\n\nSee Spell Scroll for the full rarity and level table.')
# Complete continuation paragraphs and additional entries checked on adjacent page images.
for name,extra,pages in [
 ('Pipes of the Sewers',"On a failed save, the swarm becomes Friendly to you and your allies while you continue playing each round as a Magic action. It obeys your commands; without commands it defends itself but otherwise takes no actions. If it starts its turn more than 30 feet from you, your control ends; it behaves normally and can't be swayed by the music for 24 hours.",[288,289]),
 ('Ring of Mind Shielding',"If you die while wearing the ring, your soul enters it unless it already contains a soul. You can stay in the ring or depart for the afterlife. While in it, you can communicate telepathically with any wearer, who cannot block this communication.",[296,297])]:
 _,c,a,b=DATA[name];DATA[name]=(pages,c,a,b+'\n\n'+extra)
for name in ['Spell Scroll','Cantrip Spell Scroll']+[f'Level {i} Spell Scroll' for i in range(1,10)]:
 _,c,a,b=DATA[name];DATA[name]=([308,309],c,a,b+'\n\n**Copying into a Spellbook.** A Wizard spell on a scroll can be copied into a spellbook. The copier makes an Intelligence (Arcana) check with DC 10 + the spell\'s level. A success copies the spell. The scroll is destroyed whether the check succeeds or fails.')
DATA.update({
'Ring of Protection': (297,'Ring, Rare','Yes',"While wearing the ring, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class and saving throws."),
'Ring of Regeneration': (297,'Ring, Very Rare','Yes',"While wearing the ring, you regain 1d6 Hit Points every 10 minutes if you have at least 1 Hit Point. A lost body part regrows to full functionality after 1d6 + 1 days if you have at least 1 Hit Point the entire time."),
'Ring of Resistance': (297,'Ring, Rare','No',"While wearing the ring, you have Resistance to one damage type, indicated by its gemstone. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d10.\n\n| 1d10 | Damage type | Gemstone |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Acid | Pearl |\n| 2 | Cold | Tourmaline |\n| 3 | Fire | Garnet |\n| 4 | Force | Sapphire |\n| 5 | Lightning | Citrine |\n| 6 | Necrotic | Jet |\n| 7 | Poison | Amethyst |\n| 8 | Psychic | Jade |\n| 9 | Radiant | Topaz |\n| 10 | Thunder | Spinel |"),
})
for name,armor in [('Plate Armor of Etherealness','Plate Armor'),('Half Plate Armor of Etherealness','Half Plate Armor')]:
 DATA[name]=(289,f'Armor ({armor}), Legendary','Yes',"While wearing the armor, take a Magic action and use a command word to gain the effect of Etherealness. It ends immediately if you remove the armor or take a Magic action to repeat the command word. This property recharges at the next dawn.\n\nThe book lists this under **Plate Armor of Etherealness** and permits either Half Plate Armor or Plate Armor.")
